This problem requires the Subtraction Principle, as we will need to count the total possibilities, and then subtract those that do not meet the criteria.

We have 5 marbles in total. Together each of them has 4 options (any of the rest). When picking a pair of marbles, we have 4*4 = 16 different “combinations”, if the order of selection is taken into consideration. This is because each marble can be paired with any of the other 4 marbles, including itself.

